{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>Dan shall judge his people.</b> This is Samson, who was from the tribe of Dan and was judge of Israel, and therefore it says ידין, for he was a judge and not a king. <b>As one of the tribes of Israel</b> — as the singled-out one among the tribes, namely Judah, of whom it is written ״ידך בערף אויביך״; so too this judge shall prevail over his enemies and defeat them." "<b>By way of the Midrash:</b> כאחד שבטי ישראל — like the Unique One of the world. Just as the Unique One of the world has no need for others, as it is said (Isaiah 63:3): ״פורה דרכתי לבדי ומעמים אין איש אתי ואדרכם באפי וארמסם בחמתי״, so too Samson had no need for others — not for sword, not for spear, not for bow, nor any other weapon of war, but only for the jawbone of the ass, as it is said (Judges 15:16): ״בלחי החמור הכיתי אלף איש״."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:21:32.978346662Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}